---
// Fact-forward pass (matches the corrected helical-piers-deep-dive.astro
// treatment). No MFRC method page exists for monitoring, but two related
// MFRC reference articles supplied real, verified content: concrete
// clues for when monitoring is the right first move vs. not enough
// (sharper than the previous vague "active, stable, or seasonal" line),
// and a genuinely separate topic -- what to watch AFTER a repair is
// done, which this page didn't cover at all before. Still deliberately
// shorter than the piering pages; the addition is a distinct topic, not
// padding. No misconceptions/Q&A section (dropped sitewide). [TIM: ...]
// marks spots needing real field experience.
//
// Per Tim: added floor-level surveys as a named tool (one survey is one
// data point -- it takes two or three over time to actually show a
// trend), named that TLS sells and installs crack monitors directly,
// linked the free printable Crack Gauge for DIY tracking, and added a
// new section on why starting monitoring early matters most before a
// home sale -- a sale doesn't leave room to monitor for months, so the
// earlier tracking starts, the more likely there's real data (either
// direction) by the time it's needed.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const title = 'Monitoring in New Mexico Foundation Repair | TLS Foundations';
const summary =
  'Monitoring means tracking a foundation\'s elevation or crack width over time to determine whether movement is active, stable, or seasonal -- before recommending a repair. Not every crack needs repair, and no sales-only company can recommend monitoring, since it generates no revenue. It is the legitimate answer when movement is cosmetic, stable, or seasonal, and the wrong answer when it is not.';
const description =
  'What monitoring actually involves, why it is a legitimate recommendation and not a stall tactic, and when watching is the right call versus acting now.';

const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: 'Monitoring in New Mexico Foundation Repair',
    description,
    about: description,
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'TLS Foundations' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'TLS Foundations' },
    url: 'https://www.tlsfoundations.com/monitoring-deep-dive',
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
